"""Framework and custom tool schema builders for LLM calls.

Internally every tool is an
:class:`~rasa.agents.schemas.agent_tool_schema.AgentToolSchema` (built-in
dicts, custom ``@tool`` functions, and remote MCP tools).
:func:`build_llm_tools_for_turn` returns that canonical type.
:func:`build_set_fields_tools_for_turn` returns only the ``set_fields``
schema for a follow-up extraction call.
LiteLLM/OpenAI JSON is emitted only at the provider boundary via
:func:`emit_litellm_tools` /
:meth:`AgentToolSchema.to_litellm_json_format`.

There are three groups:

Static framework tools
----------------------
Always present; schema is hard-coded.

* ``activate`` — start one of the allowed activation targets (``target_id`` enum).
  Globally routable entry ids are always listed; non-routable internal entry points
  are added only while their owning skill is active.
* ``complete`` — finish the active skill when it has prose instructions
  (not offered for ordered-block-only skills)
* ``cancel`` — abandon the active skill and emit ``SkillCancelled``
* ``listen`` — end the turn without a message, except on a text collect step,
  a voice collect step whose question has not been asked yet, post-search
  answer calls, and pending tool confirmation

Dynamic set_fields tool
-----------------------
A batch ``set_fields`` tool for every settable memory entry in the active
skill — fields flagged ``llm_settable: true`` plus every collect-step target.
Each property's value type is inferred from the matching :class:`MemoryField`;
descriptions come from the collect step or the memory entry.

Builder-defined custom tools
-----------------------------
Added when there is an active skill with loaded ``@tool`` functions.
Skill-local tools are auto-discovered from ``skill_tool_funcs`` unless gated
by ``tool_constraints``; shared tools require ``import_tools``. Schemas are
generated from Python function signatures via
:func:`build_custom_tool_schemas` and :func:`visible_custom_tool_names`.

Usage::

    schemas = build_llm_tools_for_turn(
        bootstrap=bootstrap,
        memory_values=memory_values,
        mcp_runtime=mcp_runtime,
        active_target_id="transfer_money",
        settable_fields=["amount"],
        listen_available=True,
    )
"""

